# dayflow-nudge settings, applied at INSTALL time by deploy/install.sh.
#
# Apply yours:
#   cp .env-example .env
#   edit .env -- uncomment the lines you want to change
#   re-run: ./deploy/install.sh
#
# The daemon re-reads every knob from its environment on every cycle
# and falls back to the documented default on any malformed value, so a
# typo costs you the default, never a broken agent.
#
# Every knob ships commented out: uncommenting one line is the whole
# mental model for changing a setting. Every knob the daemon offers is
# listed below; there are no others.

# DFN_DISABLE=1
#     Stop all nudging instantly. Default 0 (nudging on). Takes effect
#     on the next cycle and preserves all state.

# DFN_NOTIFIER=applet
#     Delivery channel. "applet" (the default) posts through the
#     compiled DayflowNudge.app poster; "oscript" degrades to bare
#     osascript (weaker Focus attribution).

# DFN_POLL_SECONDS=60
#     Poll interval in seconds. Default 60.

# DFN_STYLE=window
#     Nudge surface. "window" (the default) shows the centered
#     self-dismissing dialog; "notification" shows a standard macOS
#     notification.

# DFN_DAYS=mon,tue,wed,thu,fri
#     Operating days: the days the daemon may nudge. Comma-separated
#     day names, 3-letter or full, any case (mon, MONDAY, Sat).
#     Default Monday through Friday.

# DFN_QUIET_START=20:00
#     Start of the daily quiet window (no nudges from here). 24-hour
#     clock, 8:00 and 08:00 both accepted. Default 20:00.

# DFN_QUIET_END=08:00
#     End of the daily quiet window (nudging resumes at this time).
#     Must differ from the start. Default 08:00.

# DFN_DB_PATH=
#     Path to the Dayflow store to watch. Leave unset for the default
#     (~/Library/Application Support/Dayflow/chunks.sqlite). A leading
#     ~/ is expanded at install time.
